https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MixaByk1996/mattermost/commits/48276d105925a4d0028f858ae4a41407c47f205e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-28T20:00:49Z","email":"drakonard@gmail.com","name":"konard"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-28T20:00:49Z","email":"drakonard@gmail.com","name":"konard"},"message":"fix: Add database migrations and Telegram-like web frontend\n\nThis commit addresses the issues reported in Ошибки.docx:\n\n**Database Migration Fix:**\n- Added initial migration files for all Django apps (users, procurements, payments, chat)\n- Fixed \"relation ''users'' does not exist\" error by including proper migrations\n- Updated docker-compose.yml to run migrations automatically before starting the core service\n\n**Web Frontend (Telegram-like Design):**\n- Added complete CSS design system matching Telegram''s look and feel\n- Dark/light theme support with CSS variables\n- Responsive design for mobile and desktop\n- Main components: chat list, procurement slider, message area, personal cabinet\n\n**Two-Server Deployment Architecture:**\n- Added docker-compose.two-server.yml for split deployment\n- Server 1 (Chat): WebSocket server with dedicated Redis for real-time messaging\n- Server 2 (API/Bot): Core API, bot service, PostgreSQL, and Redis for caching\n- Nginx configurations for both servers with SSL support\n\n**Files Added/Modified:**\n- groupbuy-bot/core/*/migrations/ - Django migration files\n- groupbuy-bot/frontend/ - CSS, JS, and HTML templates\n- groupbuy-bot/docker-compose.two-server.yml - Two-server deployment config\n- groupbuy-bot/infrastructure/nginx/nginx-*.conf - Nginx configurations\n- groupbuy-bot/core/config/settings.py - Added frontend template and static dirs\n- groupbuy-bot/core/config/urls.py - Added frontend route\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropi